/*
 * cpu_ops.def - the HuC6280 opcode table, one row per opcode 00 to FF in order (plan 03-09; D-96, D-97, D-98, D-99).
 * One X-macro row per line, no continuation: DS_OP(opcode, mnemonic, mode, bytes, cycles, access, "cite"). The same file is read by cpu.c (metadata and dispatch, cite dropped) and by
 * scripts/opcode-check (awk, compared both ways with tests/oracle/huc6280-opcodes.tsv). Numbers and page labels only, no manual text (ER-9).
 * Provenance: transcribed from page images of the HuC6280 hardware manual H8-25 (the instruction map, read cell by cell at 300 dpi) and of the software manual instruction pages S8-n.
 * It was made without opening tests/oracle/huc6280-opcodes.tsv and without copying from the earlier hand-written switch of cpu.c. Where the printed map disagrees with an instruction page the page decides (opcodes 34 to 37, B4, B5, and the 7D mode label).
 *   opcode    two hex digits written 0xNN
 *   mnemonic  BBRn BBSn RMBn SMBn carry the bit number; TAM and TMA are the manual's TAMi and TMAi; NCP of the map is NOP; UNDEF marks the 22 undefined opcodes
 *   mode      IMPLIED ACC IMM ZP ZPX ZPY ABS ABSX ABSY IND INDX INDY ABSIND ABSINDX REL ZPREL BLK MASK IMMZP IMMZPX IMMABS IMMABSX UNDEF
 *   bytes     instruction length in bytes
 *   cycles    the base cycle count printed by the manual (a block transfer prints 17+6x: 17 is the base here and the 6 per byte is the block step of plan D-100); the adders (taken branch, T mode, decimal) live in cpu.c
 *   access    the bus offset class of D-92: NONE (no data access), READ, WRITE, RMW (one read then one write), STACK, MPR (TAM and TMA), BLOCK
 *   cite      the map page, then the instruction page when that page was read as an image for this table
 * The 22 undefined opcodes are one byte and two cycles by assumption (LED-CPU-0010): they execute as a NOP that clears T (D-96). Their row carries those values and the cite H8-25 (the empty map cell).
 */
DS_OP(0x00, UNDEF, UNDEF, 1, 2, NONE, "H8-25")
DS_OP(0x01, ORA, INDX, 2, 7, READ, "H8-25")
DS_OP(0x02, SXY, IMPLIED, 1, 3, NONE, "H8-25 S8-87")
DS_OP(0x03, ST0, IMM, 2, 4, WRITE, "H8-25 S8-80")
DS_OP(0x04, TSB, ZP, 2, 6, RMW, "H8-25 S8-103")
